Picture in Picture windows move freely between displays.

The app moves a PiP window with setFrameOrigin: while it is dragged or swiped. With "Displays have separate Spaces" on, AppKit
then adjusts the frame to the screen it is on (constrainFrameRect:toScreen:, _setFrame:fromAdjustmentToScreen:,
_setFrameAfterMove:), so the window stayed inside that screen's visible frame and could not cross a menu-bar strip to a
display above. A window with movesFreelyAcrossDisplays set skips those adjustments, as headless windows and tab-drag
move loops already do; the app settles a dropped PiP inside the usable area of the display it lands on.

--- a/components/remote_cocoa/app_shim/native_widget_mac_nswindow.h
+++ b/components/remote_cocoa/app_shim/native_widget_mac_nswindow.h
@@ -111,6 +111,8 @@
 // Whether this window is headless.
 @property(assign, nonatomic) BOOL isHeadless;
 
+@property(assign, nonatomic) BOOL movesFreelyAcrossDisplays;
+
 // Whether this window is currently being added to and removed from parent for
 // ordering.
 @property(assign, nonatomic) BOOL isShufflingForOrdering;
--- a/components/remote_cocoa/app_shim/native_widget_mac_nswindow.mm
